{"h":3396,"lines":[{"c":1,"y":0.034746760689755241,"x":0.096707818948445684,"w":0.061728394826253252,"h":0.013250883392226243,"t":"Test 4"},{"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","y":0.081272084892106689,"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.096707822594762738,"c":1,"w":0.3086419677734375},{"h":0.021810167669828795,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","w":0.82942103068033857,"y":0.1159671702200018,"c":1,"x":0.09659719453944679},{"h":0.015988372380376759,"t":"Passage 2 below.","c":1,"x":0.094650202890961876,"y":0.13662790682095505,"w":0.17078189849853515},{"w":0.39094650268554682,"t":"Changes in reading habits","h":0.024805174559109022,"y":0.1743227320705929,"c":1,"x":0.32098765389422407},{"x":0.23045268128772969,"w":0.57201644897460946,"t":"What are the implications of the way we read today?","c":1,"y":0.21366279049220327,"h":0.020436149884730526},{"y":0.25145348821293223,"t":"Look around on your next plane trip. The iPad is the new pacifier for babies and toddlers. Younger","x":0.09465021287595865,"w":0.84156377156575524,"h":0.017441860778592888,"c":1},{"t":"school-aged children read stories on smartphones; older kids don't read at all, but hunch over","y":0.27031802125142024,"w":0.80041152954101569,"x":0.094650202201342584,"h":0.016019188192342826,"c":1},{"y":0.28769140138555382,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054296,"t":"video games. Parents and other passengers read on tablets or skim a flotilla of email and news","w":0.80452677408854156,"x":0.094650193094062252},{"w":0.79218109130859371,"x":0.094650194966721418,"h":0.017500068610632802,"c":1,"y":0.30523255797969306,"t":"feeds. Unbeknown to most of us, an invisible, game-changing transformation links everyone"},{"w":0.78395060221354163,"y":0.32267441844553657,"c":1,"x":0.092592600021552493,"h":0.017441860778592999,"t":"in this picture: the neuronal circuit that underlies the brain's ability to read is subtly, rapidly"},{"x":0.094650206200245363,"w":0.82716049194335939,"c":1,"t":"changing and this has implications for everyone from the pre-reading toddler to the expert adult.","y":0.34010600696359461,"h":0.017452132715914948},{"y":0.37632508815401056,"c":1,"h":0.017667844522968212,"x":0.094650200315453598,"w":0.81275721232096343,"t":"As work in neurosciences indicates, the acquisition of literacy necessitated a new circuit in our"},{"w":0.80246912638346368,"h":0.017452132154269218,"x":0.094650203680696349,"c":1,"t":"species' brain more than 6,000 years ago. That circuit evolved from a very simple mechanism","y":0.39244186069560505},{"t":"for decoding basic information, like the number of goats in one's herd, to the present, highly","y":0.41133720914324923,"c":1,"h":0.017441860778592888,"x":0.09465020408639542,"w":0.78806584676106772},{"t":"elaborated reading brain. My research depicts how the present reading brain enables the","x":0.094650217897448957,"y":0.42873969375414356,"w":0.75308639526367183,"h":0.017481236631934904,"c":1},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"t":"development of some of our most important intellectual and affective processes: internalized","x":0.094650194983831093,"w":0.79218109130859371,"y":0.44758539481488668},{"y":0.46362995007762553,"w":0.83753814697265627,"h":0.019439427675712162,"x":0.094608845512611311,"c":1,"t":"knowledge, analogical reasoning, and inference; perspective-taking and empathy; critical analysis"},{"y":0.48110465099878497,"c":1,"x":0.094650209346305872,"h":0.017441860778592888,"w":0.80864196777343744,"t":"and the generation of insight. Research surfacing in many parts of the world now cautions that"},{"t":"each of these essential 'deep reading' processes may be under threat as we move into digital-","w":0.79629628499348959,"x":0.094650209704901345,"c":1,"h":0.018914180032215677,"y":0.49852767985210134},{"x":0.094253087047663317,"w":0.21479598999023436,"y":0.51534921888916707,"t":"based modes of reading.","h":0.019845598578031809,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.094650206599034545,"h":0.016008916255020877,"y":0.55377906962174117,"t":"This is not a simple, binary issue of print versus digital reading and technological innovation. As","w":0.82716049194335939},{"x":0.094650210369069607,"y":0.57122093008668517,"w":0.80246912638346368,"h":0.015988372380376759,"c":1,"t":"MIT scholar Sherry Turkle has written, we do not err as a society when we innovate but when"},{"t":"we ignore what we disrupt or diminish while innovating. In this hinge moment between print and","x":0.096707819151777133,"h":0.017489796111665123,"y":0.58716136605610192,"w":0.82716049194335928,"c":1},{"t":"digital cultures, society needs to confront what is diminishing in the expert reading circuit, what","c":1,"y":0.60360213876975122,"x":0.094599363248043078,"w":0.82520823160807288,"h":0.021509932123730091},{"t":"our children and older students are not developing, and what we can do about it.","y":0.62499999984043031,"x":0.094650211001885129,"w":0.68724278767903646,"h":0.01752061248527681,"c":1},{"t":"We know from research that the reading circuit is not given to human beings through a genetic","x":0.096707822674304778,"h":0.017450420819968837,"c":1,"y":0.65842167235598792,"w":0.80864196777343744},{"x":0.094650196573841758,"y":0.67726737340098031,"t":"blueprint like vision or language; it needs an environment to develop. Further, it will adapt to that","w":0.83744857788085936,"h":0.017500068610632802,"c":1},{"t":"environment's requirements - from different writing systems to the characteristics of whatever","y":0.6944646644077771,"w":0.80669896443684896,"h":0.018750842805464796,"c":1,"x":0.094597764256301384},{"y":0.71204242168524934,"t":"medium is used. If the dominant medium advantages processes that are fast, multi-task oriented","c":1,"w":0.82107650756835937,"h":0.018390408393491375,"x":0.094607435767323222},{"y":0.73110465100358191,"c":1,"h":0.017441860778592888,"x":0.094650203144078376,"w":0.79423868815104159,"t":"and well-suited for large volumes of information, like the current digital medium, so will the"},{"c":1,"t":"reading circuit. As UCLA psychologist Patricia Greenfield writes, the result is that less attention","x":0.094650198445405537,"w":0.82510289510091139,"h":0.016007204359074767,"y":0.74852767950325472},{"c":1,"y":0.76737338053556914,"t":"and time will be allocated to slower, time-demanding deep reading processes.","h":0.01751034054795475,"x":0.094650205638510745,"w":0.66666666666666663},{"x":0.094650200317199354,"c":1,"y":0.80232558124956277,"w":0.81275721232096354,"t":"Increasing reports from educators and from researchers in psychology and the humanities bear","h":0.015990084276322869},{"c":1,"y":0.81976744171420124,"x":0.094650202183492141,"t":"this out. English literature scholar and teacher Mark Edmundson describes how many college","h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.80041152954101558},{"y":0.83716136605610192,"c":1,"t":"students actively avoid the classic literature of the 19th and 20th centuries in favour of something","h":0.017489796111665123,"x":0.096707841650892773,"w":0.83127568562825516},{"t":"simpler as they no longer have the patience to read longer, denser, more difficult texts. We should","h":0.017667844522968212,"y":0.85600706731849041,"w":0.83127573649088538,"x":0.096707810664536667,"c":1},{"y":0.90697674398936357,"h":0.01453488398216074,"x":0.09670781845432487,"c":1,"t":"86","w":0.026748971939086916},{"w":0.254254862467448,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","h":0.028412784086661036,"c":1,"x":0.71947457586097274,"y":0.95563152623822323}],"w":2400}